H2("6.2   Model Selection and Layer B")
P("Table 4 shows the selection path. Among deep models, the BiLSTM had the fewest validation misses at the common threshold, and the Transformer about 2.6 times as many. Adding URL features and the rank through a boosted model then cut validation misses from 414 to 19, which is the largest single step in the system. XGBoost and LightGBM tied at 19, and the tie was broken on validation PR-AUC. The held-out columns show why a choice like this should not be over-read: LightGBM would have cleared more Vietnamese clean URLs (65.3 % against 55.1 %) at the cost of 5 more misses, and random forest missed fewer URLs on the external sets only because it cleared far fewer clean ones (19.3 % on the Vietnamese set).")
