H2("6.3   What the Gate Depends On (RQ2)")
P("The ablation gave the first warning. Over three seeds, mean validation misses rise from 18.0 to 392.7 when the Tranco rank is removed, against 29.3 without the BiLSTM score and 27.0 without hand-crafted features. Clean training URLs were partly crawled from Tranco-ranked sites, so the rank might simply encode the label.")
P("E3 tests this (Table 6, Fig. 2). The gate clears 78.6 % of ranked clean URLs on the test set and 1.0 % of unranked ones. PhreshPhish matters most here, because its clean pages were not collected from Tranco: 25.5 % of them are unranked, and only 1.6 % of those are cleared. Across the three sets, at least 99 % of cleared clean URLs are on ranked domains. In practice the gate works as a popularity allowlist refined by URL shape. A small legitimate site almost always goes to the LLM.")
